<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cambodunum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cambodunum was a Roman town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iller">Iller</a> in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raetia">Raetia</a>, on the site of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kempten">Kempten</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. Mentioned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a>, it was among the earliest Roman towns north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> and had a forum, baths and temples. Its excavated remains form an archaeological park.</p></div>
